# November 28, 2026: State hospitals and asylums of New York, a batch of the themed pass on historic public institutions
# for the mentally ill and the "feeble-minded". Utica, Willard, the Binghamton inebriate asylum, Hudson River, Harlem Valley,
# Kings Park and the Buffalo State Hospital were already on the Atlas and are not repeated here.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's articles on each institution; the National Register records for the
# Octagon and Brigham Hall; WAMC and Untapped New York on Middletown; the Rockland County Business Journal on Letchworth
# Village; Livingston County's history page on Craig Colony; Hudson Valley Ruins on Matteawan; Empire State Development's
# Gowanda feasibility study (2025) and a State Senate release on the Gowanda prison's closing; DASNY's 2024 demolition
# finding, the DEC notice and an Assembly member's release on St. Lawrence; Asylum Projects for Middletown, Gowanda,
# St. Lawrence and Brigham Hall; Michael Kleen on St. Lawrence; the College of Staten Island's Willowbrook Mile pages;
# Queens Farm's visit page.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
